-- Issue 154: uPER OCTET / BIT STRING (CONTAINING X) of 16K units or more, whose general length (X.691 10.9) has
-- fragments. A fragment of 16K .. 48K units (C1 .. C3) is the last one (10.9.3.8.1): the decoders reject a fragment
-- header after it, and a two-octet length below 128 (10.9.3.6), and accept a final length after it. The contents of
-- C32K / CV are 32768 octets / 16384 .. 32768 octets with a 15-bit length; B32K counts bits.
UPER-WIRE-CONT DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN
    O32768 ::= OCTET STRING (SIZE(32768))
    O4096  ::= OCTET STRING (SIZE(4096))
    OV     ::= OCTET STRING (SIZE(16384..32768))
    C32K   ::= OCTET STRING (CONTAINING O32768)
    B32K   ::= BIT STRING (CONTAINING O4096)
    CV     ::= OCTET STRING (CONTAINING OV)
END
